<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Iscor half-year earnings plunge, div cut.</title>
<headline>Iscor half-year earnings plunge, div cut.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year/Half year ended</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-excepts (cts)  6.5	 vs 17.6</p>
<p>    Shr, post-exceps (cts)  7.0	 vs 21.6</p>
<p>    Cap award (cts)	   3.0	 vs  4.4</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   170	   vs 501</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   257	   vs 718</p>
<p>    Net cash outflow	926	   vs 104</p>
<p>Full name: Iscor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Steel maker Iscor said it had brought its results forward three weeks since the performance was below market expectations.</p>
<p>The company said it had elected to allocate capitalisation shares in the ratio of 0.83 new shares for every 100 held. Shareholders may opt to renounce their capitalisation shares to the underwriter for the cash equivalent of 2.7 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
